    "messages": [
      "Done. All four commands ran as ordinary, separate `docker` invocations in the configured environment, with no worktree mount.\n\n## Results\n\n**1. `docker build -t app:test .`** (before repair) \u2014 exit 0. Built cleanly; the `.dockerignore` assertion in the Dockerfile passed.\n\n**2. `docker run --rm app:test`** (before repair) \u2014 **exit 1**, failed:\n```\nExpected a repaired value, received broken-opus\n```\n\n**Diagnosis:** `check.mjs` reads `value.txt`, writes `dist/result.json`, and exits 1 when the value starts with `broken-`. The file contained `broken-opus`. The image bakes the source in via `COPY . .` (no mount), so the stale value was frozen into the layer \u2014 the rebuild is what makes a fix visible.\n\n**Repair:** `value.txt` changed from `broken-opus` to `opus`. Nothing else touched \u2014 `Dockerfile` and `check.mjs` are unmodified (`git status` shows only ` M value.txt`).\n\n**3. `docker build -t app:test .`** (after repair) \u2014 exit 0, new image `sha256:95b68e3a5ff0\u2026` (previously `sha256:9deccf8835c8\u2026`).\n\n**4. `docker run --rm app:test`** (after repair) \u2014 **exit 0**, passed:\n```\nValidated opus\n```\n\n**Local `dist/result.json`:**\n```json\n{\"value\":\"opus\"}\n```\n\nNote on output sync: the failing run produced no local `dist/` \u2014 the worker only reported `output ready` on the passing run, so `dist/result.json` reflects the successful attempt. Per instructions, nothing was committed and no additional worktree was created."
